Syntax
---  (start of Ansible YAML file)
hosts: server-group    -----------------> which server this playbook run for 
become: yes    ---------------------------> use sudo / root privilege  
tasks:
   -name: task descrption
    module_name:
    parameter1: value
    parameter2: value 

some point which need to know about ansible ----
inventory playbook -- define target server
playbooks-- core automation file written in yamal
module-- ansible works using module
variable-- makes variable reusable
handler-- used for restarting services only when change occur
role-- role organise large playbook (Imp)  
template-- used for dynamic configuration file
Ansible vault-- encryption password and secrets
ad hoc command-- quick one line command
Idempotency-- ansible avoid repeating same word unnecessarily (Imp)

example 1:- install and start nginx in webserver
---
hosts: webserver
become: yes
tasks:
  -name: install nginx
   apt:
   name: nginx
   state: present
  -name: start nginx
   service:
   name: nginx
   state: present


example 2:- install, copy and start java application on appserver
---
hosts: appserver
become: yes
tasks:
  -name: install  java 
   apt:
   name: openjdk-17.jdk
   state: present 
  -name: copy jar files
   copy:
   src: app.jar
   des: /apt/app.jar
  -name:  start java application
  shell: java-jar/apt/app.jar


example 3 with Role and idempotency 
install java, install docker, install nginx, copy nginx file, deploy and run the java application on appserver
---
hosts: appserver
become: yes
roles:
       -java
          tasks:
            -name: install  java
            apt:
            name: openjdk-17.jdk
            state: present
            update_cache: yes
       -docker
          tasks:
            -name: install docker
            apt:
            name: docker.io
            state: present
            -name: docker service
